{"name":"Farmer’s Market","hex":"#8f917c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"farmer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone or something that farms, as:\nA person who works the land and/or who keeps livestock; anyone engaged in agriculture on a farm.","A person who works the land and/or who keeps livestock; anyone engaged in agriculture on a farm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/farmer"},{"term":"market","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gathering of people for the purchase and sale of merchandise, often periodic at a set time.","A relatively spacious outdoor or covered site where traders set up stalls, either temporarily or permanently or semi-permanently, and buyers browse the merchandise."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (products or services) available for sale and promote them.","To promote for or as if for sale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/market"}],"entries":[{"title":"Farmers' market","blocks":[{"text":"A farmers' market is a physical retail marketplace intended to sell foods directly by farmers to consumers. Farmers' markets may be indoors or outdoors and typically consist of booths, tables or stands where farmers sell their produce, live animals and plants, and sometimes prepared foods and beverages. Farmers' markets exist in many countries worldwide and reflect the local culture and economy. The size of the market may be just a few stalls or it may be as large as several city blocks. Due to their nature, they tend to be less rigidly regulated than retail produce shops."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Farmers_and_Artisans_Market_at_Farmington_-_Michigan.jpg/330px-Farmers_and_Artisans_Market_at_Farmington_-_Michigan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farmers'_market"},{"title":"Farmer","blocks":[{"text":"A farmer is a person engaged in agriculture, raising living organisms for food or raw materials. The term usually applies to people who do some combination of raising field crops, orchards, vineyards, poultry, or other livestock. A farmer might own the farmland or might work as a laborer on land owned by others. In most developed economies, a \"farmer\" is usually a farm owner (landowner), while employees of the farm are known as farm workers. However, in other older definitions a farmer was a person who promotes or improves the growth of plants, land, or crops or raises animals by labor and attention."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Woman_at_work%2C_Gujarat.jpg/330px-Woman_at_work%2C_Gujarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farmer"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a0/Layyah_fruit_vegetable_market.jpg/500px-Layyah_fruit_vegetable_market.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a0/Layyah_fruit_vegetable_market.jpg/500px-Layyah_fruit_vegetable_market.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A farmers' market at twilight in Layyah, Pakistan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALayyah_fruit_vegetable_market.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Garlic_for_sale_in_a_market_in_France.jpg/500px-Garlic_for_sale_in_a_market_in_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Garlic_for_sale_in_a_market_in_France.jpg/1280px-Garlic_for_sale_in_a_market_in_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Garlic_for_sale_in_a_market_in_France.jpg/500px-Garlic_for_sale_in_a_market_in_France.jpg?utm_source=e